# J9 - Codemode: sandboxed JS that chains tools in one turn

## Summary
Added the `codemode` agent tool: runs a short model-written JS program in a
sandbox (QuickJS via quickjs-emscripten WASM, with isolated-vm fallback),
with no fs/net/process/timer access; `tools.<name>(args)` routed through Loam's
existing tool registry and the same approval/policy path as normal tool calls;
CPU time and memory limits; only the script's return value (truncated to a cap)
enters the transcript. Opt-in setting, off by default.

## Files
- src/codemode/engine.ts - sandbox engine (QuickJS WASM runtime, resource limits)
- src/codemode/tool.ts - `codemode` agent tool implementation
- src/codemode/policyGate.ts - policy/approval gate for sandbox tool calls
- src/codemode/wasmLoader.ts - WASM loader (esbuild-bundled, works in build:server)
- src/codemode/index.ts - module entry point
- src/codemode/__tests__/engine.test.ts - engine tests
- src/codemode/__tests__/policyGate.test.ts - policy gate tests
- src/codemode/__tests__/tool.test.ts - tool tests
- THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES - jcode MIT notice entry
- src/config.ts - codemode config (enabled, timeoutMs, memoryBytes, maxToolCalls)

## Acceptance verified
- Script calling read+grep 20x returns a summary; transcript growth < 2 KB
- No fs/net/process access enforced
- Timeout and memory limit enforced
- Policy-denied tool stays denied
- Gates pass: tsc --noEmit, build:server (esbuild bundling of the wasm works),
  next build, new tests + existing tests for touched files

## Test commands
- node --import tsx --test src/codemode/__tests__/
- npx tsc --noEmit
- npm run build:server
- cd packages/web && npx next build